From: Zurker <91011862+hershate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:49:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Papo: vault zero-listener gate for VaultDisplayItemEvent

Every ACTIVE vault rebuilt CraftBlock + asBukkitCopy + event + asNMSCopy per
display-item cycle (every 20 ticks per vault). VaultDisplayItemEvent has its own
HandlerList and no subclasses; Cancellable defaults to false and
getDisplayItem() returns the constructor arg, so with zero listeners the event
is never cancelled and the round-trip is a content-identical fresh copy of the
rolled stack. The rolled stack is an exclusive fresh stack from the loot roll,
so passing it to setDisplayItem directly is equivalent. The loot roll itself
(vanilla display cycling) is untouched.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/vault/VaultBlockEntity.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/vault/VaultBlockEntity.java
index ecf36e261f1a50b34f0e10d9abe62bc590cc6a7c..44111aed33f96a66783ba5f94d8c2793f2d5d8b2 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/vault/VaultBlockEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/vault/VaultBlockEntity.java
@@ -307,9 +307,18 @@ public class VaultBlockEntity extends BlockEntity {
                     level, pos, config.overrideLootTableToDisplay().orElse(config.lootTable())
                 );
                 // CraftBukkit start
+                // Papo start - zero-listener fast path: VaultDisplayItemEvent has its own
+                // HandlerList and no subclasses; Cancellable defaults to false and
+                // getDisplayItem() returns the constructor arg. With zero listeners the event is
+                // never cancelled and asNMSCopy(event.getDisplayItem()) is a content-identical
+                // fresh copy of the rolled stack — which is itself an exclusive fresh stack from
+                // the loot roll, so passing it through directly is equivalent.
+                if (org.bukkit.event.block.VaultDisplayItemEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length > 0) {
+                // Papo end
                 org.bukkit.event.block.VaultDisplayItemEvent event = org.bukkit.craftbukkit.event.CraftEventFactory.callVaultDisplayItemEvent(level, pos, randomDisplayItemFromLootTable);
                 if (event.isCancelled()) return;
                 randomDisplayItemFromLootTable = org.bukkit.craftbukkit.inventory.CraftItemStack.asNMSCopy(event.getDisplayItem());
+                } // Papo - end zero-listener fast path
                 // CraftBukkit end
                 sharedData.setDisplayItem(randomDisplayItemFromLootTable);
             }
